<Doc title="Privacy Policy: Analytics, AdSense Cookies and Your Choices" description="How Macro Release Desk uses Google Analytics 4 and AdSense cookies, how consent works in the EEA, UK and Switzerland, and how to opt out of personalised ads." path="/privacy/" h1="Privacy policy" kicker="Legal · privacy" updated="2026-10-15"
  answer="We do not ask you to create an account and we do not sell personal data. Google Analytics 4 measures visits with region-specific storage defaults. AdSense ad loading is disabled pending account and consent setup.">
  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>This site, {site.domain}, is operated by the publisher of Macro Release Desk. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.</p>
  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Usage data via Google Analytics 4:</strong> pages viewed, approximate location derived from IP (GA4 does not store IP addresses), device and browser type, referrer, and events such as using a page control. We use this to understand which pages are useful.</li>
    <li><strong>Advertising data via Google AdSense:</strong> Google and its partners use cookies or similar identifiers to serve ads, limit repetition and measure performance, and, where you allow it, to personalise ads based on your visits to this and other sites.</li>
    <li><strong>Email:</strong> if you write to us, we keep your message and address to reply. We do not add you to any list.</li>
    <li><strong>Server logs:</strong> our hosting provider (Cloudflare) processes IP addresses and request data to deliver and secure the site.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Consent in the EEA, UK and Switzerland</h2>
  <p>For visitors in the EEA, UK and Switzerland, advertising and analytics storage default to denied through Google Consent Mode v2. The AdSense advertising loader is disabled until the publisher account and required certified consent management platform are verified. A consent banner is not currently configured. You can opt out of analytics through the browser settings and Google tools linked on this page.</p>
  <h2>How to opt out</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Turn off personalised ads in <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/">Google’s Ad Settings</a>, or visit <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/">aboutads.info</a> (US) and <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/">youronlinechoices.eu</a> (EU).</li>
    <li>Install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.</li>
    <li>Block or delete cookies in your browser settings.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Learn <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</p>
  <h2>Third-party vendors</h2>
  <p>Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user’s prior visits to this website or other websites. Google’s use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on visits to this site and/or other sites on the Internet.</p>
  <h2>Retention and your rights</h2>
  <p>Google Analytics retention follows the property settings; a specific retention period has not been verified. Emails are kept as long as needed to handle your request. Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete or object to processing of your personal data; write to us and we will respond within 30 days.</p>
  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>This site is not directed at children under 16 and we do not knowingly collect their data.</p>
  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We will update this page when our practices change and revise the date above.</p>
</Doc>
